    "evidence_text": "Red Symons\n\n He currently hosts ABC Radio Melbourne's breakfast show.\n\nThailand's Got Talent (season 6)\n\n Thailand is also the fifth country in Asia to license Got Talent series.\n\nSophie Monk\n\nGot Talent Portugal (season 5)\n\n Each judge can press the golden buzzer once in the auditions same as last year, such as the hosts.\n\nReece Mastin\n\n Mastin subsequently signed with Sony Music Australia.\n\n \"Good Night\" and \"Shout It Out\" earned him two ARIA No. 1 Chart Awards.\n\nAustralia's Got Talent\n\nAustralia's Got Talent is an Australian reality television talent show which premiered on 18 February 2007 on the Seven Network.\n\n The show is based on the \"Got Talent\" series format that originated in the United Kingdom with Simon Cowell.\n\n The original judges were Tom Burlinson, Red Symons and Dannii Minogue.\n\n All four judges from season seven will be replaced by Kelly Osbourne, Ian \"Dicko\" Dickson, Sophie Monk and Eddie Perfect in season eight.\n\nJon English\n\n He emigrated to Australia with his parents in 1961.\n\n The show debuted in June 2015.\n\nDan Karaty\n\n Freelusion reached the semi-finals of Britain's Got Talent in 2013.\n\n Currently, both groups are still together.",
